y all realized that  they had the word bottom  in their surnames on another occasion he  sabotaged a pretentious play in vogue in  london he bought several numbered  tickets and handed them out the bald men  thus strategically placed their pates  seen from the theater balconies spelled  a popular expletive a four-letter word  starting with s and ending in t cole  even took care of dotting the eye that's  amazing according to another version of  the prank there were only eight bald men  and they all sat in the same row but  each had a letter painted on the back of  their heads so that the audience could  clearly read b-o-l-l-o-c-k-s  not all his practical jokes were so well  planned sometimes called like to  improvise as a dead ringer for labor  leader ramsay mcdonald cole was  frequently mistaken for him once  spotting a group of railroad workers he  introduced himself to them as the  politician to their dismay he then  launched into a terrain against the  labor movement and the dangers of  socialism none of these pranks however  impressed public opinion as much as his  masterpiece the dreadnought hoax  in early 1910 cole was accosted by a  junior naval officer who was engaged in  a duel of pranks against the officers  the hms dreadnought pride of the royal  navy could he devise the ultimate trick  to humiliate his rivals cole happily  accepted enlisting the help of adrian  stephen adrian happened to have a  rivalry with his cousin william fisher  also an officer on the dreadnought so of  course he was gay the two devised a plan  similar to the zanzibar hoax and  assembled a team which included adrian's  sister virginia the parts were thus cast  horus would play the role of herbert  chalmanderlay from the foreign office  adrian i was the interpreter another  four friends decked themselves again in  turban's blackface and beards including  virginia to portray a retinue of  obsidian dignitaries they would be led  by assal mccarlen the supposed cousin of  emperor menelik on the 10th of february  1910 a telegram was dispatched admiral  may commander-in-chief of the home fleet  prince macklin of absinia and sweet  arrive at 4 20 pm today weymouth he  wishes to see dreadnought kindly arrange  meet them on arrival in repeat of the  cambridge adventure may and his other  high-ranking officers bent over  backwards to welcome the foreign  dignitaries giving them an extensive  tour of the state-of-the-art military  facility the absentian aristocrats  admired the resplendent uniforms and the  mighty guns of the dreadnought shouting  in praise bunga bunga and other assorted  gibberish when adrian was asked to  translate the admiral speech during the  tour he mangled some words in swahili  which were completely inappropriate  mixing them with latin and ancient greek  the admiral invited the epsinians to  dinner below deck but horus refused on  their behalf knowing that consuming food  would expose the fake beards as an  excuse he claimed that the princes could  not eat food that was not halal and even  asked if they could perform their muslim  prayers at sunset at a small detail  absinia now ethiopia is a largely  christian country and the hoaxes even  wore crucifixes the whole affair exposed  how ruling classes at the time had  little knowledge and consideration of  non-european cultures after the hoax  horus and adrian once again revealed all  the details of the press causing an  outcry public opinion sided with the  pranksters ridiculing the royal navy for  their gullibility and carelessness  admiral may was even subjected to a  parliamentary inquiry this was a time  when britain was competing for supremacy  of the seas against the german fleet and  the oaks had proven that it took only a  telegram and some costumes to expose  military secrets moreover it emerged  that may had squandered military funds  for a large purchase of white kids  gloves for the occasion  [Music]  the year after the dreadnought's success  horace's sister anne married a  well-known public figure future prime  minister neville chamberlain cole's  antics were a source of embarrassment  for jane berlin and eventually also  alienated his sister this may be why  cole took to spending less time in  london leading a debauched life in  continental europe and later in dublin  during one of his trips to ireland cole  fell in love with a young heiress denise  anne-marie joss lynch the two married on  september 30th 1918. he was 37 she was  barely 19. he later organized a  honeymoon which suitably took them to  venice on april fool's day 1919. he just  couldn't help himself instead of  enjoying the night with his young wife  horace spent hours dropping horse manure  all over saint mark's square again a  rather surreal stunt carried out only to  enjoy the look of confusion on the  venetians faces in a city notoriously  devoid of horses  where did it all come from once back in  ireland the trickster had some close  brushes with the ongoing independence  struggle with which cole agreed in  principle nonetheless he was still  perceived as a member of the english  oppressing aristocracy by the ira the  kohl's estate rafford was raided by the  republicans who stole cole's best  clothes and denise's jewels subsequently  the kohl's took residence in dublin's  shelbourne hotel where horus spent the  night's drinking with novelists and  painters while there cole claimed to  have identified and apprehended an  english spy who tried to mingle with the  republicans he declared to have him  arrested for his own good otherwise he  would have been shot cole sent the  alleged spy back to london with a  message claiming that the agent had been  caught by legendary most wanted  revolutionary michael collins word  spread that the trickster was somehow  linked to collins or possibly that he  was michael collins a dangerous rumor in  fact two days later cole was confronted  by two black and tans british members of  the local constabulary with a reputation  for brutality the two officers were  eager to cash the 5 000 pound reward for  the capture of collins cole displayed a  remarkable coolness when facing the  blackened hands unleashing a secret  weapon in his own words i produced some  whiskey and succeeded by lavish  hospitality and reducing the men to a  helpless state they staggered away  saying i was a jolly good fellow even if  i was michael collins and anyway  what was five thousand pounds to them  [Music]  in the late 1920s cole's bouts of low  malicious moods took over his playful  side this aspect may have alienated his  wife although biographer martin downer  points out that they were ill-matched  from the start he also became more  direct and vulgar in his jokes when the  almanac who's who asked him to submit  his entry coal filled in his recreation  as fornicating but with less letters he  was dutifully excluded things  deteriorated further in 1928 when cole  lost all his money in a bad investment  in canada denise took the occasion to  ask for a dissolution of their marriage  alone and almost penniless cole went on  voluntary exile in france while there on  the 31st of january 1931 he remarried  with mabel wright a scullery maid and  former model to painter augustus john on  the 16th of march 1935 cole and mabel  welcomed a baby boy tristan later a tv  director who also worked on doctor who  by the way at cole had access to the  tardis he would have turned back time to  prevent mabel from ever meeting augustus  john it turned out that mabel and the  painter had been having a long-standing  affair and augustus john well he was  actually the biological father of  tristan this apparently was the ultimate  prank that life had played on the  greatest trickster of his age  heartbroken impoverished and forgotten  horus veer cole succumbed to a heart  attack on february 26 1936 in hon fleur  northwestern france and thus ends the  story of the greatest pranksters he may  have left a wake of laughter behind him  but darkness always lurked close waiting  to pounce on him when the end approached  the destiny he had in common with many  are tricks to god like loki condemned to  imprisonment misery and torture but i  want to leave you on such a serious note  horus would not agree i will instead ask  you to post in the comments what is the  greatest prank you ever witnessed or  even better performed and as always  thank you for watching now just before  you leave today's video let me tell you  about another channel that i run called  decoding the unknown it's a show where i  take a deep dive in some of the world's  biggest mysteries from what happened to  the roanoke colonists the regular guy  who found a listening device in one of  his power strips it's always a bit of a  wild ride you can find a link to  decoding the unknown below or just  search decoding the unknown in youtube  and you will find it  [Music]
 

